  "body": "## Why plan first\nLetting Claude jump straight into code can solve the wrong problem well. In plan mode it reads files and runs exploring commands, then writes a plan, and your source files stay untouched until you approve. A wrong plan costs a few minutes of reading. A wrong build costs a rewind, a rebuild and a lot of tokens.\n\n## Getting in\n- **Shift+Tab** until the status line shows `⏸ plan mode on`.\n- `/plan` and the task: `/plan add saved searches per docs/prd-saved-search.md`.\n- `claude --permission-mode plan` to start a session in it.\n\n## The loop the docs recommend\n1. **Explore**, in plan mode: \"read src/search and explain how a query reaches the API.\"\n2. **Plan**, in plan mode: \"I want saved searches. Which files change? Write the plan.\"\n3. **Implement**: approve the plan; Claude builds and runs the tests.\n4. **Commit**: ask Claude to commit with a descriptive message, and open a PR when you want one.\n\n## Approving\nWhen the plan is ready, Claude asks how to go on:\n\n| Option | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| Yes, and use auto mode | Build, with the classifier checking each action. It reads \"Yes, auto-accept edits\" where auto mode is unavailable |\n| Yes, manually approve edits | Build, asking before each edit |\n| No, keep planning | Stay in plan mode and say what to change |\n\nPress **Ctrl+G** to open the plan in your editor and change it yourself before Claude goes on. With `showClearContextOnPlanAccept` on, you also get an option to approve and clear the planning conversation, so the build starts with a clean context.\n\n## When to skip it\nPlan mode adds a round trip. For a typo, a log line or a rename, ask directly. The docs' test: if you could describe the diff in one sentence, skip the plan. Plan when the approach is uncertain, when several files change, or when the code is new to you.\n\n## Plan with one model, build with another\nThe model setting `opusplan` uses Opus while you are in plan mode and switches to Sonnet to build: deep reasoning where it pays, a cheaper model for the typing.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Approving without reading. The plan is the cheapest place to catch a wrong assumption.\n- Fixing the plan in a long chat. Choose \"No, keep planning\" with the correction, or edit it with Ctrl+G.\n- Planning a whole feature at once. Plan one phase at a time ([[playbook:phase-loop|the phase loop]]).",
