  "body": "## @imports\nWrite `@path/to/file` anywhere in a CLAUDE.md and that file loads with it:\n\n```markdown\nSee @README.md for the overview and @docs/architecture.md for the services.\n\n## Git\n- Branch and commit conventions: @docs/git.md\n```\n\n- Paths are relative to the file that holds the import, and imports can nest up to four levels.\n- A path with spaces needs a backslash before each space: `@Design\\ Docs/api.md`.\n- An import inside a code span or a code block is left as text.\n- An import that points outside the project, such as a file in your home folder, asks for your approval once per project.\n- **Imports organise; they do not save context.** The imported file loads in full, every session.\n\n## .claude/rules/\nOne Markdown file per topic in `.claude/rules/`, in subfolders if you like. A rule without frontmatter loads every session, like CLAUDE.md. With a `paths` list it loads only when Claude reads or edits a matching file:\n\n```markdown\n---\npaths:\n  - \"src/api/**/*.ts\"\n---\n# API rules\n- Validate every request body with the zod schema in `src/api/schemas/`.\n- Return errors as `{ error: { code, message } }`, never as a bare string.\n```\n\n| Pattern | Matches |\n|---|---|\n| `**/*.ts` | TypeScript files in any folder |\n| `src/**/*` | everything under `src` |\n| `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | `.ts` and `.tsx` files under `src` |\n| `migrations/**` | everything under `migrations` |\n\nPersonal rules for every project go in `~/.claude/rules/`; they load before the project's rules.\n\n## The catch with path-scoped rules\nThey enter the conversation when a matching file is touched, so a compaction summarises them away, and they come back the next time a matching file is read. A rule that must always hold belongs in CLAUDE.md or in a rule without `paths`.\n\n## Where each instruction goes\n| It applies | Put it in |\n|---|---|\n| Everywhere, every session | CLAUDE.md |\n| To one kind of file or one folder | A rules file with `paths` |\n| To one task done now and then, such as a release | A skill (batch 3) |\n| Every time, without fail | A hook (batch 3) |\n\n## Monorepos\nOther teams' CLAUDE.md files above your folder can be skipped with `claudeMdExcludes` in `.claude/settings.local.json`: glob patterns matched against absolute paths. An organisation's managed CLAUDE.md cannot be excluded.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Splitting a 600-line CLAUDE.md into imports and expecting it to cost less.\n- `paths: src/api` instead of a glob such as `src/api/**`.\n- A must-always rule in a path-scoped file, lost after the next compaction.",
